---
import Page from '@layouts/Page.astro'
import {
  DOWNLOAD_URL,
  ISSUES_URL,
  MINIMUM_MACOS,
  RELEASES_URL,
  SUPPORT_EMAIL,
  withBase,
} from '@utils/site'

const description = 'Get help with Taskmato: contact support, report bugs, and find answers.'
---

<Page title="Support — Taskmato" description={description} heading="Support">
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    The fastest way to reach me is by email: <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a
    >. Taskmato is a one-person project, so please allow a few days for a reply.
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also report bugs and request features on the <a href={ISSUES_URL}
      >public GitHub issue tracker</a
    >, where you can follow their progress.
  </p>

  <h2>What to include in a report</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your macOS version</li>
    <li>Your Taskmato version and build number, found in Settings → About</li>
    <li>Steps to reproduce the issue</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>System requirements</h2>
  <p>
    Taskmato requires {MINIMUM_MACOS}. Apple Reminders access and an Obsidian vault are required
    only if you enable those providers. You can use the built-in Local provider without either one.
  </p>

  <h2>Common questions</h2>
  <details class="border-b border-gray-200">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold marker:text-gray-400">
      My Reminders aren't showing up.
    </summary>
    <p class="mt-0">
      Open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Reminders and make sure Taskmato has full access.
      Without it, Taskmato cannot load your lists or mark a reminder complete when a focus phase
      ends.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-b border-gray-200">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold marker:text-gray-400">
      My Obsidian tasks are missing.
    </summary>
    <p class="mt-0">
      Taskmato reads tasks written in <a href="https://publish.obsidian.md/tasks/Introduction"
        >Obsidian Tasks</a
      > emoji syntax. If you moved or renamed your vault folder, select it again in the Obsidian provider
      settings.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-b border-gray-200">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold marker:text-gray-400">
      Notifications aren't appearing.
    </summary>
    <p class="mt-0">
      Open System Settings → Notifications and make sure notifications are enabled for Taskmato.
      Also check whether a Focus mode, such as Do Not Disturb, is silencing them.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-b border-gray-200">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold marker:text-gray-400">
      Where does my data live?
    </summary>
    <p class="mt-0">
      The <a href={withBase('/privacy')}>privacy policy</a> explains what Taskmato stores and where.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="border-b border-gray-200">
    <summary class="cursor-pointer py-3 font-semibold marker:text-gray-400">
      Can I create tasks from a script or shortcut?
    </summary>
    <p class="mt-0">
      Yes. Use the <code>taskmato://start?title=...</code> URL to create an ad hoc task and start a focus
      session.
    </p>
  </details>

  <h2>Downloads</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={DOWNLOAD_URL} download>Download the latest version for macOS</a>, or view all versions
    on the <a href={RELEASES_URL}>Releases page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
